<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alan García</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a>–<a href="/years/2019">2019</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alan García was a Peruvian politician of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-popular-revolutionary-alliance">APRA</a> who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1985 to 1990 and from 2006 to 2011. His first government, populist and unorthodox, ended in hyperinflation, economic collapse and the growth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shining-path">Shining Path</a> insurgency. His second presidency followed free-market policies amid strong growth. He killed himself in 2019 as police arrived to arrest him in the Odebrecht corruption investigation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alan-garcia.jpg" alt="Alan García" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Asamblea Nacional del Ecuador · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20_de_Mayo_de_2011_Condecoraci%C3%B3n_al_presidente_de_la_Rep%C3%BAblica_de_Per%C3%BA,_Alan_Garc%C3%ADa_P%C3%A9rez_1_(84)_(5751855775)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>At the same time <b>Alan García</b>’s first government ended in hyperinflation.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-peru">Republic of Peru · Into the Present</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-12.06,-77.04&amp;year=1994" aria-label="Lima on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2433 2613 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Alan García"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2883 2883h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2883 2883h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-12.06,-77.04&amp;year=1994">What was here in 1994? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
